  After a quick source dive:

    - "spestudied" is the record field incremented when a spellbook
is read or poly'd.

    - I can't find where the "spestudied" is set to 0 when a spellbook 
is blanked.  

    - That doesn't really matter because I can't even find where 
"spestudied" is reset when a spellbook is *written*.



  Further investigation shows that:

    - "spestudied" is actually overloaded onto the "corpsenm" field.
      (See the fairly recent thread where it was discovered that
       the "warned" and "trapped" fields are the same.)

    - The "corpsenm" field is quite a busy little animal.



  It's a bloody good question that I wish I could figure out the
answer to.

  I can't even come up with a good way to test this in wizard mode,
given, as you say, that there's no easy way in-game to determine
the number of reads left in a spellbook.


  The good news is that it doesn't really matter in your current
case.  There's just one spellbook you really want.  Getting it
by polying just means you'll have to write the spellbook in order
to refresh the spell.  


  It most likely will mean that you can wish for a magic marker
to write a replacement spellbook rather than have to wish for
the spellbook directly.  And you'll have plenty of extra charges
left on that magic marker afterwards.


